ROLE SEPARATION AUDIT

architect_executor_roles_separated: true
architect_plan_graph_boundary_preserved: true
executor_resultproposal_boundary_preserved: true
gt_advisory_only: true
root_only_finaloutput_authority_preserved: true

Role separation after Phase 2:

- Architect designs PlanGraph and stops there.
- Executor performs bounded node execution and returns ResultProposal.
- Fractal DAG orders valid DAG node execution and returns boundary artifacts.
- Post V&V consumes ResultProposal boundary artifacts.
- GT is advisory and cannot create FinalOutput.
- Root remains the only FinalOutput authority.


RESULTPROPOSAL-SHAPED BOUNDARY AUDIT

resultproposal_shaped_boundary_distinction_documented: true
schema_valid_executor_resultproposal_distinguished_from_proof_boundary_artifact: true
resultproposal_shaped_is_finaloutput: false
resultproposal_shaped_is_authority: false
resultproposal_shaped_is_accepted_evidence: false
resultproposal_shaped_authorizes_action: false
resultproposal_shaped_writes_drs: false
normalization_layer_deferred: true

Boundary meaning:

- Active `hedgehog/executor.py` emits schema-valid ResultProposal objects.
- Proof-level Fractal DAG / child-cell reports may emit ResultProposal-shaped
  boundary artifacts.
- ResultProposal-shaped boundary artifacts do not create FinalOutput.
- ResultProposal-shaped boundary artifacts do not transfer authority.
- ResultProposal-shaped boundary artifacts do not create accepted evidence.
- ResultProposal-shaped boundary artifacts do not authorize action.
- ResultProposal-shaped boundary artifacts do not write DRS.
- This distinction remains until a later normalization/runtime validation layer.


